{
 "_doc": "Loki, boss (GAME_DESIGN.md: Midgard's Edge bosses; art 10/31/2026). Built by tools/art/build_boss_loki.py; rules in docs/ART_RULES.md. From Snorri Sturluson's Prose Edda: 'pleasing and handsome in appearance, evil in character, very changeable in his ways' (Gylfaginning 33), and the dwarf Brokkr sewing his lips shut (Skaldskaparmal 35), the stitched mouth carved on the Snaptun stone (Denmark, about 1000 AD). Viking Age dress from finds such as Birka and Hedeby: a knee-length tunic with a woven border, a cloak pinned at the shoulder, trousers with leg wraps, leather shoes. The flame in his hand is his wildfire attack. Not based on any modern version (GAME_DESIGN.md: never Marvel's Loki: no horned helmet, no green and gold).",
